{"acceptedClaimRefs":[{"assessmentDigest":"sha256:2f9288bc1e1ee62ec02d6bc967ddfe961e693b1c3d15b2e42ec4a4dc421d0e47","claimKey":"bssc-sum-capacity/uv-relaxed-converse-tensorization","judgmentId":"sha256:34c5377dbd5c5d147acb250ac80640770b6176749e6c235d4a71ebc508b615c2","transactionId":"14889884ae6ac1f80cc56485e7acf1b0b2cb6ae9"}],"acceptedClaims":[{"claimKey":"bssc-sum-capacity/uv-relaxed-converse-tensorization","dependencyTransactionIds":["c70e1829a7c6a2a8cb8cfc2383f8abf825ac5ea6"],"statement":"For finite-alphabet discrete memoryless broadcast channels, the averaged separately-relaxed UV sum-rate functional defined in this contribution is exactly additive under products. On a receiver-skew channel the branchwise functional equals the averaged functional, and the same equality and additivity hold for every finite product of receiver-skew channels. Consequently, for the half-skew BSSC P and every integer n >= 1, both functionals on P^{times n} equal n(2 h_2(1/4) - 5/4) bits. This is a theorem only about the two separately-relaxed scalar UV functionals, not about tensorization of the full UV region, a common joint-(U,V) optimization, the GK functional, or the capacity itself."}],"evidenceChunkDigests":["sha256:0d46c2dbd1a62f0385fc4d8878d8cfef3749f85cca019e1284c5e54c12016874","sha256:96375d4961d1ed5f5f5b3da368e59c60c4bd0fc6779b741a484b40f2114db4a2","sha256:c4df63434cb0c5f76918bd0ba578629f7373d4f2b24d6d6b5e21d3c253f2e852","sha256:d0dce591c90e6b529890b34e4bd515167ea3c447daef11e95f28e1c5f3c328d2"],"evidenceManifest":{"chunkSizeBytes":65536,"contributionPath":"problems/bssc-sum-capacity/contributions/uv-relaxed-converse-tensorization","files":[{"bytes":7416,"chunks":[{"bytes":7416,"digest":"sha256:c4df63434cb0c5f76918bd0ba578629f7373d4f2b24d6d6b5e21d3c253f2e852","offset":0,"ordinal":0}],"digest":"sha256:c4df63434cb0c5f76918bd0ba578629f7373d4f2b24d6d6b5e21d3c253f2e852","path":"problems/bssc-sum-capacity/contributions/uv-relaxed-converse-tensorization/README.md"},{"bytes":938,"